<!--
  Deliberately empty, and it must stay that way.

  Two capture paths live in this module, and neither belongs here:

  1. SMS User Consent, the default. It needs no permission at all: play
     services shows the user a dialog for each candidate message, and the app
     only ever sees a message the user approved.

  2. Auto-read, which does need a receiver, a service, and the RECEIVE_SMS
     permission. Those are added by the `withOtpSmsAutoRead` config plugin in
     `app.config.ts`, and only in a build made with OTP_SMS_AUTOREAD=1.
     Declaring them here would put them in every build unconditionally, which
     takes that choice away — the single thing that plugin exists to preserve.

  So if a *_SMS permission, receiver, or service ever appears in this file,
  something has regressed and must be reverted.
